<title>HONG KONG: HK observatory reports 5.8 quake in Philippines.</title>
<headline>HK observatory reports 5.8 quake in Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>An intense earthquake estimated at 5.8 on the Richter scale was detected east of the Philippines early on Friday, Hong Kong's Royal Observatory said.</p>
<p>The observatory said the epicentre of the quake, detected at 0222 local time (1822 GMT), was located about 330 km (206 miles) east of Cebu.</p>
